%% A parameter bound to an input type at a bare occurrence (TGLP,
%% parameterized-types.tex, Definition "Instantiation"): echo(C?, D) is
%% well-typed at X = Choice? and at no output binding, so X = Choice? is the
%% binding considered.  The definition also asks that the clauses of echo be
%% well-typed at echo(Choice?, Choice), and echo(X?, X) is not: its moded head
%% has the writer X at the consumed position 1 (well-typing.tex, Definitions
%% "Moded Head" and "Consistent Paths"), and Lemma "Parametricity" certifies
%% a parameter replaced by a type of the same mode only.  So no binding makes
%% the clause and echo's clauses well-typed, and the call is refused (TGLP
%% appendix-implementation-notes.tex, "The instantiation of a call", cc4a891),
%% echo's head named at the binding; until 2026-10-02 the program was refused
%% at echo's head alone.
%% Fixture of glp_runtime/test/analysis/input_binding_test.dart.

Choice ::= yes ; no.

procedure(X) echo(X, X?).
echo(X?, X).

procedure go(Choice?, Choice).
go(C, D?) :- echo(C?, D).
